[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Accelerated London System, Steinitz Countergambit"]
[ECO "D00"]
[Character "sharp,tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,pin"]
[Themes "b2-pressure,nb5-c7"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2...c5 3.e3 Qb6"]
[Start "london-bf4-first 3.e3"]

3... Qb6 ( 3... Nc6 4. c3 Nf6 ( 4... Bf5 5. Qb3 { Hits b7 and d5 together, now that the bishop has left c8. } ) ( 4... e6 { Transposes to 2...e6 3.e3 c5 4.c3 Nc6. } ) ( 4... cxd4 5. exd4 ) 5. Nd2 ) ( 3... cxd4 4. exd4 Nc6 ( 4... Nf6 5. c3 ) ( 4... Bf5 5. c3 ) ( 4... e6 5. Nf3 ) 5. c3 ) ( 3... c4 4. b3 { Breaks up Black's queenside pawns before they gain more space. } ) ( 3... e6 { Transposes to 2...e6 3.e3 c5. } ) ( 3... Nf6 4. Nd2 ) 4. Nc3 { Counterattacks: the knight hits d5, and if the queen grabs b2, Nxd5 threatens Nc7+ and Rb1 together. } 4... e6 ( 4... c4 5. Nxd5 { The d5 pawn was only defended by the queen's pin on b2. After ...Qa5+ White has won a pawn and keeps the better game. } ) 5. Nb5 { Threatens Nc7+, forking the king and the rook on a8. } 5... Na6 6. a4 { Stops ...Nb4 and ...Nc7 ideas and keeps the knight on b5 firmly placed. } 6... Nf6 7. Nf3 { Develops and keeps c3 free for a pawn that supports the centre. } 7... Be7 8. c3 { Takes b4 away from Black's pieces. Then Bd3 and castle: b2 is no longer a worry because the queen and rook cover it. } *
